In a previous article, coutu@cithe303.cithep.caltech.edu (Stephane Coutu) says:

>
>By the time she ascended, my character had the following intrinsics:
>fast                      (started fast + ate a Q + wore speed boots)

	[Impressive intrinsic list deleted]

	If I'm not mistaken (and that sure has happened before, but
I just checked this out in Wizard Mode) eating a quantum mechanic
when you are already fast makes you slow. Eating one when you're
slow makes you fast, though.
	Perhaps I misunderstood you; maybe you ate a Q corpse
by accident, or because you were starving, and you just wanted
to let us in on all the sordid details. If that's the case, then
the aforementioned sordid details are appriciated.
	Incedentally, if you are fast (via wand of speed, or inherent
or earned intrinsic) and then put on speed boots, the game says
"You feel yourself speed up a bit more." Does this actually increase
your speed at all? It sure doesn't seem to give you any advantage
in combat, although the first speedup you get certainly does (you
get twice many attacks, or your opponents attack half as often,
depending on the your point of view.) What about earning the speed
intrinsic when already fast? For example, a Valkyrie can zap herself
with a wand of speed (one speedup), wear speed boots (two speedups),
and then earn the speed intrinsic by advancing to experience level
seven (for a whopping three speedups). How fast is the resulting 
character, really? Does some kind source-code-owning person know?
